      "text": "Overall, PFAS destruction in our treatment train showed comparable or better results than these reported methods for IX still bottom treatment, and adding iodide to the UV/sulfite treatment may further improve defluorination. 3.4.5. Energy consumption, limitations, and future studies The Electrical Energy per Order (EE/O) (kWh/m 3 ) for PFAS degra - dation in the still bottoms via UV/sulfite treatment is in the range of 18.8 \u2013 35.1 kWh/m 3 in the still bottoms, or 0.9 \u2013 1.8 kWh/m 3 in the original water treated, except for PFBS, which was recalcitrant to UV/ sulfite degradation. Detailed calculations are presented in Section S9 in the SI. While this study is the first step proof of the concept of the treatment train, there is still room to improve the performance using more aggressive UV/sulfite conditions if 100 % PFAS defluorination is necessary. Future studies should also evaluate the treatment train using packed-bed resins with continuous flow to fully utilize resin capacity before regeneration. In such more realistic settings, much higher con - centrations of PFAS and other components (e.g., DOM and anions) will be enriched in still bottoms. Both performance evaluation and energy"
